<article class="env-lemma" id="0CVA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CVA">Lemma <span data-tag="0CVA">77.2.4</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0CV6" data-tag="0CV6">77.2.1</a>. Let $(Y_1, y_1) \to (Y, y)$ be a morphism of pointed algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume $Y_1 \to Y$ is flat at $y_1$. If $(T \to Y, t' \leadsto t, \xi )$ is an impurity of $\mathcal{F}$ above $y$, then there exists an impurity $(T_1 \to Y_1, t_1' \leadsto t_1, \xi _1)$ of the pullback $\mathcal{F}_1$ of $\mathcal{F}$ to $X_1 = Y_1 \times _ Y X$ over $y_1$ such that $T_1$ is étale over $Y_1 \times _ Y T$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose an étale morphism $T_1 \to Y_1 \times _ Y T$ where $T_1$ is a scheme and let $t_1 \in T_1$ be a point mapping to $y_1$ and $t$. It is possible to find a pair $(T_1, t_1)$ like this by Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03H4" data-tag="03H4">66.4.3</a>. The morphism of schemes $T_1 \to T$ is flat at $t_1$ (use Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03MO" data-tag="03MO">67.30.4</a> and the definition of flat morphisms of algebraic spaces) there exists a specialization $t'_1 \leadsto t_1$ lying over $t' \leadsto t$, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/03HV" data-tag="03HV">29.26.9</a>. Choose a point $\xi _1 \in |X_{T_1}|$ mapping to $t'_1$ and $\xi $ with $\xi _1 \in \text{Ass}_{X_{T_1}/T_1}(\mathcal{F}_{T_1})$. point of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\kappa (t'_1) \otimes _{\kappa (t')} \kappa (\xi ))$. This is possible by Divisors on Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CV2" data-tag="0CV2">71.4.7</a>. As the closure $Z_1$ of $\{ \xi _1\} $ in $|X_{T_1}|$ maps into the closure of $\{ \xi \} $ in $|X_ T|$ we conclude that the image of $Z_1$ in $|T_1|$ cannot contain $t_1$. Hence $(T_1 \to Y_1, t'_1 \leadsto t_1, \xi _1)$ is an impurity of $\mathcal{F}_1$ above $Y_1$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
